Data Architecture

Design and evolve a fit-for-purpose data and analytics architecture.

A well-designed data and analytics architecture can help you reduce complexity, cost, and technical debt while enabling you to gain actionable insights from exponentially growing data volumes. Adopt a layered and modular architecture that will allow you to use the right tool for the right job as well as iteratively and incrementally evolve your architecture to meet emerging requirements and use cases.

Based on your requirements, select key technologies for each of your architectural layers, including ingestion, storage, catalog, processing, and consumption. To simplify ongoing management, consider adopting serverless technologies. Focus on supporting real-time data processing, and consider adopting a Lake House architecture to facilitate data movements between data lakes and purpose-built data stores.